    narr:generatedFrom "d451297a6dd1dbdf2eecccafc5b2a8b4c1a89a3a" ;
    narr:narration """This position holds the sequencing debate for multi-site cutovers, and the arc runs from judgment to constraint to external ratification — while remaining formally contested. The mainline opens as [a firm one-site-at-a-time stance with a clean soak before the next site](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_8), restated as [a settled decision to sequence singly](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_16) and compressed to [the bare one-at-a-time rule](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_6). The counterweight is [the case for pairing two sites sharing a dispatch desk](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_12), met by [the rota-problem-versus-staffing-problem rebuttal](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_15) and [the contained-pain-with-a-named-owner trade](narr:Expr_1HalyardWeekly20260908_13). The arithmetic layer lands hard: [a supervisor-count showing a same-week double cutover strips the region's rota](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_11), capped by [the flat claim that the people don't exist](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_12) and [the reframing from risk to arithmetic](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_14), which [the technical rules silently assuming one open cutover window](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_25) reinforce. A review adds a scoping note: [the sequential plan unchanged while an adjacent number is corrected](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_10), with [agreement that only the soak figure was wrong](narr:Expr_4HalyardCutoverReview20260915_11). New since the last digest, an outside advisor layer arrives: [a four-site plan summary restating the sequence](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_3), [advice to hold the approach against pressure](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_4), [precedent from three programmes where big-bang went backwards](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_5), [a warning that pressure to collapse the sequence arrives dressed as efficiency](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_7), and [a directive to write the reasons down now](narr:Expr_6HalyardAdvisorTonyMaley20260929_9). But review acts still contest the settled reading: [an acceptance of the change into this position](narr:Expr_3ReviewEvents70102_2) sits beside [a rejection arguing the call settled on two sites in parallel](narr:Expr_3ReviewEvents70102_4) and [a change request saying containment did not settle the sequencing](narr:Expr_3ReviewEvents70102_3). The register runs antithesis-first with parallelism and metaphor behind it.""" ;
